{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Therefore whoever kills Cain.</b> The plain sense of the verse is thus: because Cain was worried that he would be killed, the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: whoever kills Cain — after seven [generations] I will avenge his killer. And according to this, the meaning of the ensuing verse, ״ויאמר למך לנשיו״, is that Lamech was lamenting over himself: ״כי איש הרגתי לפצעי״ — this is Cain, who was tall in stature and advanced in years. לפצעי — לחבורתי, that is, for my injury, and for my death, for the Holy One, blessed be He, said: ״שבעתים יוקם כל הורג קין״, and Lamech — seventy-seven. And if so, even if Lamech begets seventy-seven sons, all of them will die for that sin."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:02.988349533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}